I can confirm the issue. To clarify, it's specific to GDScript, the same property hints work fine in the Inspector or for _VisualScript. The problem is that GDScript doesn't seem to handle `PROPERTY_HINT_RESOURCE_TYPE` with multiple possible types. A workaround could be to use `Resource` in such case but I couldn't locate the code responsible for handling this hint.

I found this, but it doesn't solve the issue, the real problem seems to be deeper in the parser/analyzer.
```diff
diff --git a/modules/gdscript/gdscript_editor.cpp b/modules/gdscript/gdscript_editor.cpp
index 504c7414f6..c31d368c1d 100644
--- a/modules/gdscript/gdscript_editor.cpp
+++ b/modules/gdscript/gdscript_editor.cpp
@@ -517,7 +517,13 @@ static String _get_visual_datatype(const PropertyInfo &p_info, bool p_is_arg = t
 
        if (p_info.type == Variant::OBJECT) {
                if (p_info.hint == PROPERTY_HINT_RESOURCE_TYPE) {
-                       return p_info.hint_string;
+                       if (p_info.hint_string.find(",") != -1) {
+                               // Multiple possible types but we only want one result. Could look
+                               // for first common parent type, but let's hardcore Resource for now.
+                               return "Resource";
+                       } else {
+                               return p_info.hint_string;
+                       }
                } else {
                        return p_info.class_name.operator String();
                }
```
